      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/2/13/14",
      "text": [
        " رِوَايَةِ اِبْنِ أَبِي نَصْرٍ عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ اَلْقَمَّاطِ : أَنَّهُ سُئِلَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَمَّنْ أَجْنَبَ فِي أَوَّلِ اَللَّيْلِ فِي شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ فَنَامَ حَتَّى أَصْبَحَ قَالَ «لاَ شَيْءَ عَلَيْهِ وَ ذَلِكَ أَنَّ جَنَابَتَهُ كَانَتْ فِي وَقْتٍ حَلاَلٍ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1897 - In the narration of Ibn Abi Nasr from Abu Sa'id al-Qammat:\nAbu Abdullah (as) was asked about someone who became junub (in a state of ritual impurity) at the beginning of the night in the Month of Ramadan and then slept until morning.\nImam (as) said: \"There is no penalty upon him, as his state of janabah occurred during a permissible time.\""
        ]
      }
